# K03d: the book's spelling at the unit's root -- `copy: merge Model` declares the merge result at the
# unit's top level, and `read` names the free `copy\value`.  By the general priority of a free name's
# sources the method's hidden input is that result (K02c, MERGE-HIDDEN-INPUT-PROJECTION), so read
# returns 1.  This is the shape steps/k03-head-roles-20261001.md recorded as blocking K03's last item
# ("`w: merge Model` inside a method is still unresolved name"): before this slice a unit-level atom
# tail was silently read as a NAMED STRUCTURE named copy, and its atoms never became a merge.
# Success is 7.
Model: (int: value 1)
copy: merge Model
fn: read () int
return: copy\value

int: result read()
if: result != 1
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 81; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
